	'k28b8afd8' => 'Rafael Duarte directs component purchasing for a regional agricultural machinery manufacturer, managing vendor relations across fabricated metal, hydraulics, and machined parts. He advocates for regional machining suppliers to mitigate supply disruption and maintain responsive quality feedback loops. At Renkei Forum 2027, Rafael opens Friday morning with Sec.07, focusing on buying components close to home. Later that afternoon, he co-presents Sec.11 with Amara Nwosu, sharing industrial buyer perspectives on structuring transparent call-off schedules within multi-year supply frameworks.',
	'k298b85b9' => 'Calder Hall opens its doors at 08:30 on both event days. On Thursday 13 May 2027, morning presentations in Hall A commence at 09:00, with activities concluding after the supplier reception at 18:30. On Friday 14 May 2027, doors open at 08:30, sessions run from 09:00 to 16:15, and the venue closes at 16:30 following the closing address. The registration desk operates continuously throughout these hours to assist delegates.',
	'k298e2d5d' => 'Chen Wei-Lin is the founder of an established contract textiles workshop producing industrial garments and institutional linens. Having navigated rigorous commercial tendering for regional healthcare and hospitality clients, she specialises in drafting workable supply agreements for small manufacturing facilities. During Renkei Forum 2027, Chen leads Sec.04 on Thursday afternoon, detailing uniform contracts for small workshops. Her presentation outlines standard terms, minimum order thresholds, and realistic production lead times that protect small manufacturers while meeting corporate delivery expectations.',
