	'k7dd9e1e0' => 'Mirela Novak is a freight and logistics planner specialising in consolidated transport networks across regional manufacturing corridors. She works alongside suppliers and local distributors to organise shared freight runs, reducing deadhead miles and lowering distribution overheads for small producers. At the forum, Mirela presents Sec.05 on Thursday afternoon, titled Shared deliveries. Her session demonstrates how non-competing producers in adjacent sectors can combine regional delivery routes, maintain consistent delivery timetables, and satisfy stringent receiving dock requirements without operating dedicated truck fleets.',
