	'k86ec1832' => 'Complimentary two-day buyer delegate passes (€0) are strictly reserved for commercial buyers, category procurement managers, institutional purchasing directors, and municipal sourcing officers. During registration, applicants must detail their purchasing remits, relevant commodity categories, and approximate procurement requirements. Our team reviews these details to confirm that delegates have active purchasing responsibilities. Once approved, buyer delegates receive full access to all 12 sessions in Hall A, lunch on both days, and up to 8 meeting requests across the four matching rounds.',
	'k88615592' => 'Invoicing details',
	'k887fd88a' => 'Renkei Forum 2027 provides regional producers with direct, pre-scheduled access to 160 commercial and municipal buyers. Choose between delegate attendance passes or dedicated exhibition tables in the Calder Hall foyer.',
	'k88870675' => 'At Renkei Forum 2026, representatives from the city kitchen procurement office sat down with several regional produce growers to discuss municipal catering requirements. Historically, the municipality had tendered food procurement as a single large contract that excluded smaller agricultural producers unable to supply the entire city&#039;s volume. Following discussions at the forum regarding procurement barriers, the city kitchen procurement team restructured their upcoming catering tender, splitting the single contract into 4 accessible lots based on seasonal crop categories and geographical delivery zones. This structural adjustment enabled two local agricultural growers to submit competitive bids. Both growers secured supply lots for seasonal vegetables, supplying the city kitchen with fresh produce while the municipal administration achieved greater procurement diversity and reduced freight transit across its catering supply chain.',
	'k8913b656' => 'Programme',
	'k8936c5c0' => 'Opening: why regional',
	'k894e58ba' => 'How a city office turned one large tender into lots that small suppliers can bid for.',
