	'kee6b3f88' => 'The empty grey-seated auditorium at Calder Hall in daylight before a session.',
	'kef26403e' => 'Every participant arrives with a reviewed commercial profile and pre-arranged appointments. You know who is sitting across the table, which contracts they manage and what capacity they need before the doors open.',
	'keff3f1f0' => 'Talks, meeting rounds, lunch both days (after profile review)',
	'kf04c7bb8' => 'Case 02',
	'kf0e21e01' => 'Pass from €180. Table with 2 passes €1,450.',
	'kf2a90ceb' => 'Doors reopen at 08:30 for the second forum day. Proceedings in Hall A commence at 09:00 with Sec.07, in which Rafael Duarte examines regional procurement for industrial machinery components. At 09:40, Sophie Brandt delivers Sec.08 on first-time food-safety audit compliance. Kofi Mensah follows at 10:30 with Sec.09, outlining commercial payment terms that sustain supplier cash flow. Meeting round 3 occupies Hall B from 11:15 to 12:45. After lunch, Ilse Varga leads Sec.10 at 14:00 on drafting supplier profiles that procurement teams evaluate effectively. At 14:40, Amara Nwosu and Rafael Duarte co-present Sec.11, reviewing frameworks and call-off orders. Meeting round 4 runs from 15:15 to 16:15, leading into Sec.12 at 16:15 for closing reflections and next steps before doors close at 16:30.',
	'kf3453ce4' => 'specifications',
	'kf497c238' => 'and cancellation',
	'kf5629a68' => 'buyers',
	'kf656ccbd' => 'Speakers',
	'kf6f16494' => 'Amara Nwosu leads supplier development within the Northport city procurement office, designing frameworks that enable small and medium-sized suppliers to participate in public contracts. She works extensively on unbundling large institutional tenders into competitive commercial lots. At the forum, Amara delivers Sec.02 on Thursday morning, focusing on practical techniques for splitting municipal tenders into accessible lots. On Friday afternoon, she joins Rafael Duarte in Hall A for Sec.11, examining how framework agreements and call-off orders function under municipal procurement guidelines.',
	'kf750245a' => 'Who qualifies for the free buyer pass?',
	'kf8eb1e45' => 'Can suppliers arrange meetings outside the four designated rounds?',
	'kf93c3512' => 'What we heard, what happens next and how to join the 2028 waitlist.',
	'kfa2bfdc9' => 'A buyer and a supplier talk at a small table with samples and a notebook.',
	'kfa734f8d' => 'All registered two-day and one-day passes for buyers and suppliers include morning coffee, afternoon refreshments, and a full seated lunch served in the foyer and dining area on the relevant forum days. Catering is supplied using regional ingredients sourced through cooperative agricultural suppliers. Vegetarian and common dietary options are standard. Observer ticket holders do not receive catering services but can access municipal cafes and dining establishments located along Wharf Road within walking distance of the venue.',
	'kfa8ac10a' => 'Hall B',
	'kfaba582b' => 'Day 1',
	'kfb15f522' => 'Observer passes are available for €60, providing two-day access exclusively for public-sector personnel, researchers, and university students studying supply chain logistics and economics. Observer passes allow admission to Hall A to hear all 12 speaker presentations, observe open Q&amp;A panels, and explore the foyer exhibition area. Observer tickets do not include participation in Hall B one-to-one matching tables, meeting request submissions, or delegate catering, ensuring that matching tables remain dedicated to commercial negotiations.',
	'kfbb4d0f2' => 'Public-sector staff and students, talks only',
	'kfc254ecd' => 'Sec.03',
	'kfc4c9522' => 'Reception 17:30–18:30 in the foyer.',
	'kfcdc2d5f' => 'Doors open at Calder Hall at 08:30. The morning begins in Hall A with Sec.01 at 09:00, where forum director Ilse Varga presents the opening keynote on regional procurement. At 09:40, Amara Nwosu leads Sec.02 on splitting public tenders into accessible lots. Tomás Ferreira presents Sec.03 at 10:30, addressing packaging supply chains operating within an 80-kilometre radius. Meeting round 1 runs from 11:15 to 12:45 across Hall B. Following lunch, afternoon sessions resume at 14:00 with Sec.04 by Chen Wei-Lin on uniform contracts for small workshops, followed by Sec.05 at 14:45 with Mirela Novak discussing shared regional deliveries. Meeting round 2 takes place from 15:30 to 17:00. The day concludes with Sec.06, an open Q&amp;A panel at 17:00, before the evening supplier reception runs from 17:30 to 18:30 in the foyer. Doors close at 18:30.',
